{
  "configuration_id": "config_010",
  "reason": "We have only one data point (config_001: RNA-only, single-profile, PCA → 48.5% acc), so the most critical uncertainty is whether the image modality carries useful signal for this task at all. config_010 (image_only, singleprofile, resnet50) is a clean, single-variable comparison to config_001: same profile setting (single), same architectural simplicity (no aggregation/fusion), differing only in modality. This isolates the effect of switching from RNA to image features. If image accuracy is comparable or higher, it strongly motivates multimodal fusion experiments later; if it is much lower, it suggests RNA is the dominant signal and we should prioritize RNA encoder/aggregation improvements. This is the highest-information next step because it calibrates the value of the image modality before committing budget to more complex multimodal configurations, and it avoids changing multiple design axes simultaneously."
}

